Subject: [PATCH 06/61] LPM.ratio/UPM.ratio: define the 0/0 case at degree > 0

For degree > 0 the ratio LPM/(LPM+UPM) is 0/0 when every observation
equals the target, so NNS.CDF(rep(2,4), 1) and NNS.CDF(2, 1) were all
NaN. Return the degree-0 ratio there (the degree -> 0 limit and the ECDF
convention x <= target): LPM ratio 1, UPM ratio 0. Documented in the
@return of both functions (roxygen in partial_moments_rcpp.cpp, RcppExports.R
and the Rd files).

Before -> after:
  LPM.ratio(1, 3, rep(3,4))       NaN -> 1
  UPM.ratio(1, 3, rep(3,4))       NaN -> 0
  NNS.CDF(rep(2,4), 1)$CDF        NaN NaN NaN NaN -> 1 1 1 1

Only targets with zero total deviation change; all other values are
identical (checked LPM.ratio(1, sort(x), x) against LPM/(LPM+UPM)).
